Subject: [PATCH 10805/11171] [outer-loop] Count client request timeouts in
 channel_totals (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6890)

The 2026-09-02 gate run lost two 2400s timeouts to the record: channel_totals
stayed ALL ZERO and last_generated_tokens=-1, indistinguishable from a run
that never called the generator, while the server log held the real numbers
(24,942 / 26,563 tokens, truncated=0). New request_timeouts key in
_EMPTY_CHANNEL_TOTALS, incremented at both request-failure seams (generate()
and complete_text) when the exception is timeout-shaped (_is_timeout_error:
bare TimeoutError, or URLError wrapping one -- both observed shapes).
Non-timeout failures do not increment it (n_server_failures already counts
those; SCENARIO-6890-B pins the distinction).

Mutation-proven: neutering the generate()-seam increment turns both
parametrized generate tests RED; restored byte-identical (cmp), 5/5 green.
The teardown memory-watchdog error in test_arc_induction_diagnosis_6710 is
pre-existing (reproduces against HEAD's unmodified module) and unrelated.

Mutation-gate marker 2f1d7b1fb25a deleted deliberately: every listed path was
tagged NOT-this-run -- my own uncommitted spec/module edits (authored, the
content of THIS commit) plus two results/ files from the conductor's in-flight
work, untouched here. The tests fake urlopen and write nothing tracked.

